    kind: work_item  # e2bc
    title: "verify-claims: YAML loader silently drops unknown fields (typos like 'constrant'/'must-not-exist'); resulting 'inconclusive' verdict indistinguishable from no-checker-available"  # e2bc
    status: todo_hard  # e2bc
    priority: 2  # e2bc
    parent: INV-fabov-kapit-mupit-tigoz-lurol-mulus-jivik-kajun  # e2bc
    tags:  # e2bc
    - dogfooding  # e2bc
    - verify_claims  # e2bc
    - fold_audit_2026_06_03  # e2bc
    isbefore: []  # e2bc
    duplicate_of: []  # e2bc
    not_duplicate_of: []  # e2bc
    pr_ref:  # e2bc
    description: "## Origin\n\nMaterialized 2026-06-04 from the 2026-06-03 fold-audit (Family E). Stand-alone finding F31.4 previously folded onto INV-fabov. Full evidence remains on INV-fabov's pass-31 discussion entry; this row provides discrete representation.\n\n## Symptom\n\n`verify-claims` YAML loader silently drops unknown fields at `load_claims`. The resulting `inconclusive` verdict (\"No machine-checkable constraint on this claim\") is indistinguishable from the legitimate \"constraint genuinely lacks a checker\" case.\n\n**Test sequence (pass-31).** Four YAMLs filed against /tmp/hg-dogfood-s21/bm.json:\n\n| Variant | Cause |\n|---|---|\n| 1. `kind: must_exist`, `pattern:`, `description:` | All field names use spec-narrative wording that doesn't map to load_claims() at verify_claims.py:218-225 |\n| 2. `constrant.must_not_exist` (typo `constrant`) | top-level constraint key typo |\n| 3. `constraint.must-not-exist` (hyphen instead of underscore) | sub-field key-style typo |\n| 4. Mixed-case YAML key | similar shape |\n\nAll four return verdict `inconclusive` with details `\"No machine-checkable constraint on this claim\"`. The verdict is the SAME the loader produces for genuinely-not-checkable claims, so the consumer cannot distinguish:\n\n- (a) The YAML is structurally correct but the constraint genuinely lacks a checker (correct verdict).\n- (b) The YAML has typos / unrecognized fields and was silently dropped at parse time (incorrect — should warn).\n\n## Mechanism\n\n`verify_claims.py:188-228` (`load_claims`) does:\n```python\nentry.get(\"id\", \"\")\nentry.get(\"text\", \"\")\nconstraint.get(\"boundary\", \"\")\nconstraint.get(\"must_not_exist\", False)\n```\n\nNo validation that all keys in `entry` or `constraint` are recognized; unknown keys silently ignored; the resulting `Claim` is populated with defaults. The dataclass field default for `must_not_exist` is `False`, so typo'd-key claims register as \"has no constraint\" → verdict `inconclusive`.\n\n## Causal context\n\nThis is the OTHER half of INV-bitig's Phase 3 PR4 fix. PR4 closed silent-CONFIRM by introducing `ClaimVerdict.inconclusive`. That closed the empty-source-dir fall-through (silent-confirm → silent-inconclusive). But the YAML-load layer also silently drops typos AND emits `inconclusive` — so a security analyst can't tell their typo'd claim from a \"no checker available\" verdict.\n\nSibling row WI-verify-claims-silent-confirm-on-unknown-boundary catches a DIFFERENT post-PR4 residual: unknown boundary-axis values still silently confirm (not inconclusive). This row catches the typo-in-YAML-keys case at the load layer.\n\n## Invariant\n\n`verify-claims` YAML loader validates every top-level entry key AND every `constraint` sub-key against an allowlist. Unknown keys produce one of:\n\n1. **rc=2 at load** with `Error: unknown YAML field '<key>' in claim '<id>' (allowed: [...])` — preferred, catches typos before processing.\n2. **Verdict `inconclusive`** with reason `\"YAML field '<X>' not recognized; possible typo\"` (preserves stream continuity).\n\nPath (1) is stricter. Path (2) needs `details` discrimination from the legitimate-no-checker case (different reason text).\n\n## Fix sketch\n\nAdd field-name allowlists at `verify_claims.py:188-228`:\n\n```python\nALLOWED_ENTRY_KEYS = {'id', 'text', 'constraint', 'evidence', ...}\nALLOWED_CONSTRAINT_KEYS = {'boundary', 'must_not_exist', 'must_exist', ...}\n\nfor entry in data.get('claims', []):\n    unknown = set(entry.keys()) - ALLOWED_ENTRY_KEYS\n    if unknown:\n        raise CLIError(\n            f\"Error: unknown YAML field(s) {unknown} in claim '{entry.get('id', '?')}'\"\n        )\n    ...\n```\n\nSame registry-membership pattern as WI-verify-claims-silent-confirm-on-unknown-boundary (Family E sibling); the two fixes share the same load-time-validation gate.\n\n## Source provenance\n\n- **F31.4** — INV-fabov discussion entry 2026-06-02T07:33:27 (pass-31; paragraph beginning \"Pass-31 face: verify-claims YAML silently accepts unrecognized fields\").\n\nLab notebook: pass 31 under `~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/`.\n\n## Related rows\n\n- Parent: **INV-fabov** (META: Command-line arguments and configuration values silently accepted) — natural umbrella.\n- Sibling: **WI-verify-claims-silent-confirm-on-unknown-boundary** (Family E — different post-PR4 residual; same load-time-validation gate).\n- Sibling: **WI-verify-claims-yaml-shape-validation** (Family D — different YAML failure mode; shape vs key-name validation).\n- Cousin: **INV-bitig** (closed — empty-source-dir fall-through; Phase 3 PR4 partially addressed this family).\n- Sibling: **INV-murig** (registry-membership META; analogous fix-pattern)."  # e2bc
    fields: {}  # e2bc
